From d854afa3b2d36e4b599eac070f1585752bc89364 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kalmarv <59708937+Kalmarv@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 16:17:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Video-memory arenas: D32S8 and MSAA targets get heaps of
 their own size, let go when unused

The arenas (for GPU-owned textures the driver will not make reserved: D32S8 /
R32G8X24, MSAA) were heaps of at least 256 MiB at 256 MiB boundaries, so the
retail game's D32S8 targets, spread over 3.5 GB of its addresses, took
2.8 GB (HANDOFF, "Retail game bring-up", open item). A placement that
straddled arenas made a union arena while the old ones lived on.

Now an arena is a heap of its placement's size (64 KiB, or 4 MiB for MSAA,
alignment). A placement at an arena's addresses (inside it, at an offset its
alignment allows) shares it; any other gets its own, so there are no unions.
Arenas count their resources and one unused for 2 s is let go, as target
pages are.

Tests: the arena bookkeeping on its own (sharing, sizes, the 2 s release,
and the title's streaming pattern of back-to-back targets placed again over
3.5 GB, which stays bounded), and on the GPU 14 D32S8 3840x2160 targets
256 MiB apart, a clear + CopyResource + read of both planes, and the release.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 327c24c98ea883f9fa586d647b5898e073ca6d34)
